{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Peter Adebayo Odesola","identifier":"doi:10.1101/2025.09.28.25336834","title":"Model uncertainty quantification: A post hoc calibration approach for heart disease prediction","year":2025},"claim":"Isotonic calibration significantly improves probability calibration metrics such as Brier score and Expected Calibration Error (ECE) for tree ensemble models like random forest and naive Bayes.","concepts":["calibration","random forest","isotonic regression","brier score"],"id":"E1","quote":"Isotonic calibration consistently improved probability quality for most models: random forest Brier from 0.007 to 0.002, ECE 0.051 to 0.011, log loss 0.056 to 0.012; naive Bayes Brier from 0.162 to 0.132, ECE 0.145 to 0.118, log loss 1.936 to 0.446; SVM ECE 0.086 to 0.044 and log loss 0.142 to 0.133.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"751fc87d51f0a2325316551cb1fedb58435bc7f9eea4879e6c08ee9dc43757f4","kind":"artefact","prev":"5b42ca5be746755ab96574afa4e533cfda6a43c30fcb2ff3cff2025312de4455","seq":12,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T05:54:18.537+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Dhruv Nigam","identifier":"doi:10.1145/3703323.3703330","title":"ForeCal: Random Forest-based Calibration for DNNs","year":2024},"claim":"A Random Forest-based calibration method (ForeCal) improves calibration performance (ECE) while having minimal impact on the model's discriminative ability (AUC).","concepts":["calibration","random forest","isotonic regression","brier score"],"id":"E2","quote":"Through experiments on 43 diverse datasets from the UCI ML repository, we show that ForeCal outperforms existing methods in terms of Expected Calibration Error(ECE) with minimal impact on the discriminative power of the base DNN as measured by AUC.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"bd7d075300ebb9aea9f4f4fef1ecbe0dec5a775de9da580a66263c39bc0c9848","kind":"artefact","prev":"751fc87d51f0a2325316551cb1fedb58435bc7f9eea4879e6c08ee9dc43757f4","seq":13,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T05:54:18.537+00:00"}
